ed cross-runtime\n523:unsupported outcomes. B7 additionally requires cycle-safe manifests and\n524:dependency closure. Neither changes the projection fingerprint or establishes\n529:The VM does not build a second lossless record DAG. Named datoms remain the\n530:lossless source, and lexical positions, binder diagnostics, and provenance are\n532:require its own design and is outside B0 through B7.\n546:2. D2 lossless DAG: drop it from B0 through B7 and make it a non-goal. Named\n559:   projection fingerprint is never H.\n566:8. D8 committed B6: closed images are fetched by H over `dao.stream`, verified\n574:11. D11 free names: before B7, sharing is safe only for closed images or\n576:    errors, and B6 may refuse non-closed images.\n580:- B6 request/response schema and contract stamps.\n581:- B7 dependency-closure and SCC manifest mechanics.\n591:named storage, projection algorithm, and projection fingerprint remain\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
